The map z: R -> R³ defined by 

		z(t) = (acos(t), asin(t), bt), a,b constants (a > 0)

is called a circular helix, so named because its projection in the xy-plane is a circle of radius a. 
THe helix itself lies in the right circular cylinder x² + y² = a² (Figure 3.3). 
The value of b determines how tightly the helix twists. 

